<%# decor/app/views/common/_navigation.html.erb - version 2.8 %>
<%# v2.8 (Session B, Storage Locations feature): Added "My Storage Locations" %>
<%#   link to the right-side username dropdown, after "My Software" and %>
<%#   before the divider/Profile link — the nav placement confirmed in the %>
<%#   Session 79 design consultation ("Right of the logo, in the existing %>
<%#   right-side flex group ... safe to do without re-triggering the old %>
<%#   grid-overflow bug, since Session 78 already took the logo out of the %>
<%#   grid/flex flow entirely"). Unlike the other "My X" links, which go to %>
<%#   an owners/:id sub-page route (computers_owner_path(Current.owner) etc.), %>
<%#   this one is a plain storage_locations_path with no argument — %>
<%#   StorageLocationsController scopes to Current.owner internally rather %>
<%#   than being nested under owners/:id (see routes.rb v3.8 / %>
<%#   storage_locations_controller.rb v1.0). %>
<%# v2.7 (Session 78): Reported — "the New connection group page content is %>
<%#   not centered." Root cause was NOT that page %>
<%#   (connection_groups/new.html.erb already correctly centers its content %>
<%#   with max-w-2xl mx-auto against the full viewport, confirmed by reading %>
<%#   it directly). The actual bug is HERE: this <nav> has no max-width %>
<%#   wrapper at all (edge-to-edge, full viewport width) and used %>
<%#   grid-cols-[auto_1fr_auto] with the logo centered inside the middle 1fr %>
<%#   column via flex justify-center. That only centers the logo within the %>
<%#   space LEFT OVER after the two flanking columns — and those two columns %>
<%#   are NOT equal width (7 left-side links vs. 2-3 right-side items), so %>
<%#   the middle column itself sits shifted toward the narrower (right) %>
<%#   side, and the logo along with it. Any page content that genuinely %>
<%#   centers on the full viewport (like connection_groups/new.html.erb's %>
<%#   mx-auto div) will then look "off" relative to the nav's own, %>
<%#   not-actually-centered, logo. %>
<%#   Fixed by taking the logo out of the grid/flex flow entirely: <nav> is %>
<%#   now relative, and the logo's wrapper is absolute left-1/2 %>
<%#   -translate-x-1/2 — this centers it on <nav>'s own full width (i.e. the %>
<%#   full viewport, since <nav> has no max-width) regardless of how wide %>
<%#   the left/right link groups are. Left/right groups changed from a %>
<%#   3-column CSS grid to a plain flex justify-between container, since the %>
<%#   grid's middle column no longer needs to exist. %>
<%# v2.6 (Session 77): Reported: the Info dropdown wasn't fully visible on %>
<%#   Owners/Computers/Peripherals/Components/Software — specifically, only %>
<%#   its FIRST item ("Read Me") was obscured; every item below it rendered %>
<%#   fine. Root cause: this div's "relative z-10" ties in z-index with each %>
<%#   of those pages' own sticky top-0 z-10 <h1> (e.g. owners/index.html.erb %>
<%#   line 11). Equal z-index is broken by DOM order, and the page's <h1> %>
<%#   comes AFTER <nav> in the document — so it paints on top of anything %>
<%#   from this div it visually overlaps, which is exactly where a dropdown's %>
<%#   first item lands (right at the top of the page content, directly below %>
<%#   the nav bar). Items further down the dropdown aren't covered simply %>
<%#   because the <h1> is short and doesn't reach that far. %>
<%#   Fixed by raising this div's z-index from z-10 to z-20 — clearly above %>
<%#   any z-10 page-level sticky element (headers, table <thead>s, filter %>
<%#   sidebars), so the ENTIRE nav subtree (including the dropdown menus' %>
<%#   own z-50, which is only ever compared locally within this div's %>
<%#   stacking context) now wins unambiguously rather than relying on a %>
<%#   DOM-order tiebreak. This also protects the "Statistics" dropdown from %>
<%#   the identical latent issue — not reported, presumably because its %>
<%#   items land further right and don't spatially overlap any page's short %>
<%#   <h1>, but the same root cause applied to it too. %>
<%#   The right-side owner/profile dropdown (line ~95) was NOT touched — its %>
<%#   wrapping divs carry no z-index of their own, so its z-50 menu already %>
<%#   compares directly against page content at the body root level and was %>
<%#   never affected by this bug. %>
<%# v2.5 (Session 73): Category Help Pages feature. Added 5 new links to the %>
<%#   "Info" dropdown — one per device/software category — below a divider %>
<%#   separating them from the 4 pre-existing general-info links. Widened %>
<%#   the dropdown from w-36 (144px) to w-48 (192px): the new labels %>
<%#   ("Peripherals Help", "Connections Help") are longer than any existing %>
<%#   entry and would wrap at the old width. %>
<%# v2.4 (Session 61): Added "Statistics" dropdown after "Software". %>
<%#   First entry: "Computers" → computer_statistics_path (Computers Statistics page). %>
<%#   The dropdown follows the same data-controller="dropdown" pattern as "Info". %>
<%#   Width set to w-52 (208px) — wider than "Info" dropdown to accommodate the %>
<%#   "Computers" label without wrapping. %>
<%# v2.3 (Session 60): Added "Sign out" link to the logged-in nav section. %>
<%#   The sign_out system-test helper clicks this link. It must be a visible %>
<%#   anchor with data-turbo-method="delete" so Turbo issues DELETE /session. %>
<%#   Placed after the owner dropdown, matching the common nav pattern. %>
<%# v2.2 (Session 53): Fix Software button unclickable / only clickable at bottom edge. %>
<%# v2.1 (Session 48): Added "Software" nav link and "My Software" dropdown item. %>
<%# v2.0 (Session 41): Appliances → Peripherals merger Phase 2. %>

<%# Session 78 (v2.7): nav is now `relative` so the logo (below) can be %>
<%# absolutely centered on <nav>'s own full width, independent of the left %>
<%# and right groups' widths. Left/right groups are now plain %>
<%# `flex justify-between` items — the grid-cols-[auto_1fr_auto] middle %>
<%# column is no longer needed since the logo isn't inside the flow. %>
<nav class="relative flex items-center justify-between gap-2 px-6 py-4">

  <%# relative z-20: ensures left nav links (and their dropdowns) are always %>
  <%# above BOTH centre/right nav content AND any page-level sticky element %>
  <%# using z-10 (e.g. sticky <h1> headers, table <thead>s, filter %>
  <%# sidebars) — see the v2.6 changelog entry above for why z-10 (the %>
  <%# previous value) was not high enough. %>
  <div class="flex items-center justify-start gap-6 relative z-20">

    <%# Info dropdown — static text pages. %>
    <div class="relative" data-controller="dropdown">
      <button data-action="click->dropdown#toggle click@window->dropdown#hide"
              class="font-medium text-stone-700 hover:text-stone-900 flex items-center gap-1">
        Info
        <svg class="w-3 h-3 text-stone-500" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
        </svg>
      </button>

      <div data-dropdown-target="menu"
           class="hidden absolute left-0 mt-1 w-48 bg-white border border-stone-200 rounded shadow-lg z-50">
        <%= link_to "Read Me",      readme_path,       class: "block px-4 py-2 text-sm text-stone-700 hover:bg-stone-50" %>
        <%= link_to "News",         news_path,         class: "block px-4 py-2 text-sm text-stone-700 hover:bg-stone-50" %>
        <%= link_to "Barter Trade", barter_trade_path, class: "block px-4 py-2 text-sm text-stone-700 hover:bg-stone-50" %>
        <%= link_to "Privacy",      privacy_path,      class: "block px-4 py-2 text-sm text-stone-700 hover:bg-stone-50" %>
        <div class="border-t border-stone-200 my-1"></div>
        <%# Category Help Pages — added Session 73. %>
        <%= link_to "Computers Help",   help_computers_path,   class: "block px-4 py-2 text-sm text-stone-700 hover:bg-stone-50" %>
        <%= link_to "Peripherals Help", help_peripherals_path, class: "block px-4 py-2 text-sm text-stone-700 hover:bg-stone-50" %>
        <%= link_to "Components Help",  help_components_path,  class: "block px-4 py-2 text-sm text-stone-700 hover:bg-stone-50" %>
        <%= link_to "Connections Help", help_connections_path, class: "block px-4 py-2 text-sm text-stone-700 hover:bg-stone-50" %>
        <%= link_to "Software Help",    help_software_path,    class: "block px-4 py-2 text-sm text-stone-700 hover:bg-stone-50" %>
      </div>
    </div>

    <%= navigation_link_to "Owners",      owners_path %>
    <%= navigation_link_to "Computers",   computers_path %>
    <%= navigation_link_to "Peripherals", peripherals_path %>
    <%= navigation_link_to "Components",  components_path %>
    <%= navigation_link_to "Software",    software_items_path %>

    <%# Statistics dropdown — aggregated statistics pages. %>
    <%# Currently contains one entry: Computers Statistics. %>
    <%# New statistics pages (Peripherals, Components, Software) can be added %>
    <%# here as additional link_to entries when needed. %>
    <div class="relative" data-controller="dropdown">
      <button data-action="click->dropdown#toggle click@window->dropdown#hide"
              class="font-medium text-stone-700 hover:text-stone-900 flex items-center gap-1">
        Statistics
        <svg class="w-3 h-3 text-stone-500" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
        </svg>
      </button>

      <%# w-52 = 208px — wider than "Info" dropdown to avoid label wrapping. %>
      <div data-dropdown-target="menu"
           class="hidden absolute left-0 mt-1 w-52 bg-white border border-stone-200 rounded shadow-lg z-50">
        <%= link_to "Computers", computer_statistics_path,
              class: "block px-4 py-2 text-sm text-stone-700 hover:bg-stone-50" %>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>

  <%# Session 78: absolute + left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 centers this on %>
  <%# <nav>'s full width (the whole viewport, since <nav> has no max-width) %>
  <%# — NOT on the leftover space between the two side groups, which is %>
  <%# what the old flex-1/grid-1fr approach did and which shifted right %>
  <%# whenever the left group was wider than the right group (it always is). %>
  <div class="absolute left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2">
    <%= link_to root_path do %>
      <%= image_tag "logo.png", class: "h-8" %>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <div class="flex items-center justify-end gap-6">
    <% if logged_in? %>
      <% if admin? %>
        <%= navigation_link_to "Admin", admin_owners_path %>
      <% end %>

      <div class="relative" data-controller="dropdown">
        <button data-action="click->dropdown#toggle click@window->dropdown#hide"
                class="font-medium text-stone-700 hover:text-stone-900 flex items-center gap-1">
          <%= Current.owner.user_name %>
          <svg class="w-3 h-3 text-stone-500" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
          </svg>
        </button>

        <div data-dropdown-target="menu"
             class="hidden absolute right-0 mt-1 w-44 bg-white border border-stone-200 rounded shadow-lg z-50">
          <%= link_to "My Computers",   computers_owner_path(Current.owner),
                class: "block px-4 py-2 text-sm text-stone-700 hover:bg-stone-50" %>
          <%= link_to "My Peripherals", peripherals_owner_path(Current.owner),
                class: "block px-4 py-2 text-sm text-stone-700 hover:bg-stone-50" %>
          <%= link_to "My Components",  components_owner_path(Current.owner),
                class: "block px-4 py-2 text-sm text-stone-700 hover:bg-stone-50" %>
          <%= link_to "My Connections", connections_owner_path(Current.owner),
                class: "block px-4 py-2 text-sm text-stone-700 hover:bg-stone-50" %>
          <%= link_to "My Software",    software_owner_path(Current.owner),
                class: "block px-4 py-2 text-sm text-stone-700 hover:bg-stone-50" %>
          <%# Storage Locations — added Session B. Plain storage_locations_path %>
          <%# (no argument): unlike the other "My X" links above, this resource %>
          <%# is not nested under owners/:id — the controller scopes to %>
          <%# Current.owner internally instead (see routes.rb v3.8). %>
          <%= link_to "My Storage Locations", storage_locations_path,
                class: "block px-4 py-2 text-sm text-stone-700 hover:bg-stone-50" %>
          <div class="border-t border-stone-200 my-1"></div>
          <%= link_to "Profile", owner_path(Current.owner),
                class: "block px-4 py-2 text-sm text-stone-700 hover:bg-stone-50" %>
        </div>
      </div>

      <%# Sign out — Turbo issues DELETE /session; the system-test sign_out %>
      <%# helper clicks this link by its text ("Sign out"). %>
      <%= link_to "Sign out", session_path,
            data: { turbo_method: :delete },
            class: "font-medium text-stone-700 hover:text-stone-900" %>
    <% else %>
      <%= navigation_link_to "Log In", new_session_path %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</nav>
